==Strategy==
This is essentially a [[:Category:Cats with Surge Immunity|Surge-immune unit]] check. As long as you have decent Surge-immune units, this stage shouldn’t be too difficult.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Esoteric Uril]] - Immune to Surges, and has insane crowd-control potential against [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku enemies]], making him the perfect choice for this stage. Beware if using him with non-Surge-immune units, as he'll trigger a lot of [[Counter-Surge]]s.
*[[Talents|Talented]] [[Li'l Lizard Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l King Dragon Cat]] - Great source of damage here as a Surge-immune spammable backliner.
*[[:Category:Anti-Aku Cats|Anti-Aku]]/Surge Immune meatshields (i.e. [[Maize Cat (Rare Cat)|Cone Cat]], Talented [[Boogie Cat (Special Cat)|Gato Amigo]], [[Ancient Egg: N003 (Special Cat)|Cat Cactus]], etc.): No -brainer units to run here. Cone Cat in particular may not be as useful if you are using a large number of [[:Category:Surge Attack Cats|Surge Attackers]].
*[[Rugby Cat (Rare Cat)|Gridiron Cat]] - If boosted, is a good option here due to targeting both traits present on this level as well as having Surge Immunity.
*[[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]] - Useful for the Doge Darks and both Gory variants, though he is vulnerable to Surges, unlike Gridiron.
*[[Ancient Egg: N109 (Rare Cat)|Barrel Cat]] - Surge Immunity and Aku Resistance combine to make it one of the best options for breaking the Malevolent King Dragon Cats' [[Shield]]s.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*Surge-immune backliners: [[Child of Destiny Phono (Uber Rare Cat)|King of Destiny]]/[[King of Doom Phono (Uber Rare Cat)|Extinction Phono(a)]], [[Kasli the Bane (Uber Rare Cat)|Kasli, Daughter of Chaos]] and [[Amakusa Shiro (Uber Rare Cat)|Amakusa]] will be able to deal very well with basically everything in the stage here.
*[[Oda Nobunaga (Uber Rare Cat)|Phantasmal Nobunaga]] - Only useful in his [[Ultra Form]], he can copy the Surge from Malevolent Macho Leg Cat and essentially freeze the entire field, save for a few, non-threatening enemies. He can also Freeze the enemies with his own attack, coming in with over 100% uptime on the Freeze.

==Trivia==
*Treacherous Road appears to be a mistranslation. Its Japanese name (悪逆無道 ''Akugyaku Mudō'') is a four-kanji set phrase that refers to extreme evil and roughly translates to "Heinous Injustice", but the word 無道 ''mudō'' (injustice) contains 道, the kanji for "path", "way" or "road", which seems to be where the "Road" in the stage's English name comes from.

